decisions:
  - id: no-bridge
    decision: Direct import of symphony-loader instead of dynamic import bridge
    rationale: Unlike Sentinel (separate @a-company/sentinel package requiring dynamic import), symphony-loader is already in paradigm-mcp which is a direct dependency. No bridge needed.
  - id: blurb-on-poll
    decision: Status blurb piggybacked on poll heartbeat rather than separate endpoint
    rationale: Agents already call paradigm_symphony_poll regularly via /loop. Adding status param there means zero extra calls. updateAgentStatus() available for standalone use if needed.
  - id: intent-color-categories
    decision: 6 intent color categories mapped from Symphony spec visualization hints
    rationale: Groups 15+ intents into visual categories (dialogue=blue, action=component, outcome=orange, system=red, lifecycle=aspect, transfer=green) for scannable conversation view.
